Z||000021||Oreif||11-13-2001||09:04 AM||||I hate when you spend over a year on a program at work and some fool puts an idiot manager in charge who has no clue what he's doing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I hate it when the same manager puts other people in charge who have no organization and are so pig-headed, that the program falls on it's face. Especially when all those above can see what is happening but do nothing to stop the madness.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>(no flame's intended to pigs)<BR>(Glad I transferred to a different program)<P>I hate "those" people who stick the front of there car into traffic so people have to stop to avoid hitting them and then they pull out in front of you.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>(By "those" there is a specific attached but I would prefer not to name it.)<P>I hate it when someone buys a Fiero and doesn't take care of it. You slowly watch the car fall apart. (Actually this applies to any car that someone buys and doesn't take care of it)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><P>I hate not being able to buy all the good looking Fiero's I find for sale.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>(Anyone have the winning PowerBall numbers? Big Lotto? A Million Dollars they don't need?)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000022||Jaygee79||11-13-2001||10:11 AM||||I hate customers who work at a bank and can't even count money.<P>I hate customers who threaten the store manager's life because she wouldn't give them a discount on something and then come in and expect us to treat them nicely.<P>I hate customers who can clearly see that you're busy cashing someone out and have a line of 5 people waiting, and they want to know if you can let them into the fitting room or if you can let their kid into the bathroom.<P>I hate customers who follow you around the store coughing on you and then say "i hope that other girl (way on the other side of the store) over there doesn't get my cold"<P>I hate customers who try on every single coat we have and leave them all unzipped.  Or those that will take stuff off the hangers and leave them on top of the racks.  Or those who can't bother to hang the clothes the way they're supposed to be hung.  Or those who will just put the clothes back after they've tried them on.  Just give them to us so we can hang them right and put them back where they're supposed to go.  Less to do at night.<P>I hate customers who buy $500 worth of clothes and then return $475 of it, or customers who return every single thing they buy.  They should just try the stuff on first.  The fitting rooms are there for a reason.<P>I hate customers who, their first time there, spend $10 on a shirt and then if they don't get an extra discount on it like they want they say "I'm one of your best customers and if you don't give me 75 cents more off I won't come here anymore."  Like I care.  Please, take your 10 bucks somewhere else and let me go wait on the lady who will be spending $750 here today.<P>I hate customers who see our sign on the door that says "if the door is locked please ring the bell" so they try the door, it's locked.  they ring the bell and we let them in.  then they come in and say "i think your door is stuck.  I couldn't get it open."  idiots.<P>I hate customers who can't even see the sign on the door that is right in front of their eyes.  They pull on the door, it doesn't open.  so they take a step back, not sure what to do with themselves, and look at the store hours (which are about 2 inches from the big sign that says ring the bell).  then they just stand there staring in the window for 20 minutes.<P>I hate customers who will read the sign and ring the bell and then not open the door.  they just wait there and keep ringing the bell every 30 seconds.<P>I hate customers who ring the bell and then come in and say "Are you closed?"  If we were closed would we have opened the door for you?  Probably not.<P>I hate customers who want to play "Let's Make A Deal."  This isn't a used car lot.<P>I hate customers who snap their fingers at you and expect you to come running to their aid.<p>[This message has been edited by Jaygee79 (edited 11-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000023||Voytek||11-13-2001||05:51 PM||||Um, you let people into the store through a normally closed door, after they ring a bell?  Do they also have a password?  What kind of 'store' is this, anyway?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I hate it when the local junkyard gets a Fiero and the car is picked clean within a few days.  Where are all those vultures coming from??  Most people wouldn't admit to owning one, but somehow there is always plenty of idiots to strip one to the frame.<P>I also hate it when they break other parts while removing the parts they want.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>I hate it when kids simply stick out their arm in front of them and proceed to walk across the street w/o waiting for cars to go by first.  WTF???  Who's teaching them this crap?  I guess I hate the people who teach the kids, too.<P>Oh, and I also hate the host of The Weakest Link.  Can you say 'YOU ARE' veeery slowly and then 'THE WEAKEST LINK' as fast as you can?  You get the idea.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000024||Black86SE||11-13-2001||07:14 PM||||I hate it when people steal things from where you work, then try to return those items without a reciept. BUT, we already know that they steal stuff and when we won't return the items without the reciept they call you a "little SH!T" like they deserve the money they rightfully stole from you. But you are on your game and call the other stores that your store owner owns (I work at a hardware and the owner owns another store of the same type within 5 miles of you) and tell them what happened and that person tries to return that item there and they are denied also. Boo-yeah! That part makes me feel good though. <P>FieroJoe will back me up on this and probably add some of his own! We work together.<p>[This message has been edited by Black86SE (edited 11-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000025||DaRkLoRD||11-13-2001||07:35 PM||||I hate when people assume you have exactly the same opinions on things as they do, and then treat you like some sort of idiot or freak when you don't..<P>there are a lot of things I disagree with, but I usually don't say anything cause it's against the general opinion..<P>relating to the above statement... I like mustangs.. and MR2s.. and talons.. and preludes.. and trans ams.. and supras.. and corvettes.. and integras.. and grand prix GTPs.. and RX7s.. and 3000GTs.. and porsches.. and ferrari 360s..<BR>basically, I like cars. There are some I dislike, but those ones are quite often very popular with people, so I get negative responses if I say I dislike them. I don't assume everyone I meet likes fieros, but I've met people who actled like I was a complete idiot because I didn't like the kind of car they prefer.<P><BR>this pet peeve goes WAY beyond cars though.. cars are in fact a very minor thing with this. religion is probably the biggest, but I'm gonna avoid that one. heh<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||4
